---
import StarlightPage from '@astrojs/starlight/components/StarlightPage.astro';

import '../styles/data-tool.css';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---

<StarlightPage
  frontmatter={{
    title: 'Compare Your Data',
    description: 'Put two vMenu transfer codes side by side, see what is different, and merge them into one new code.',
    tableOfContents: false,
  }}
>
  <p>
    Got two transfer codes, for example one from each server you play on? Paste them in below to see
    what is only in one of them, what is in both, and what is different. Then pick what to keep and
    get one new code with everything in it. If you do not have a code yet,{' '}
    <a href={`${base}/moving-your-data/`}>Moving Your Data</a> explains how to get one out of the game.
  </p>

  <div class="vmt not-content">
    <div class="vmt-sides">
      <div class="vmt-panel">
        <label class="vmt-label" for="vmc-code-left">Left code</label>
        <textarea id="vmc-code-left" class="vmt-code" spellcheck="false" autocomplete="off" placeholder="VME1G:..."></textarea>
        <div class="vmt-actions">
          <button id="vmc-pick-left" class="vmt-button" type="button">Open a text file</button>
          <input id="vmc-file-left" class="vmt-file" type="file" accept=".txt,.json,text/plain" />
          <span id="vmc-status-left" class="vmt-status"></span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="vmt-panel">
        <label class="vmt-label" for="vmc-code-right">Right code</label>
        <textarea id="vmc-code-right" class="vmt-code" spellcheck="false" autocomplete="off" placeholder="VME1G:..."></textarea>
        <div class="vmt-actions">
          <button id="vmc-pick-right" class="vmt-button" type="button">Open a text file</button>
          <input id="vmc-file-right" class="vmt-file" type="file" accept=".txt,.json,text/plain" />
          <span id="vmc-status-right" class="vmt-status"></span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="vmt-actions">
      <button id="vmc-load" class="vmt-button vmt-primary" type="button">Compare</button>
      <span id="vmc-status" class="vmt-status"></span>
    </div>

    <div id="vmc-result" class="vmt-result" hidden>
      <div class="vmt-panel">
        <div id="vmc-summary"></div>
        <div class="vmt-actions vmt-stack">
          <label class="vmt-check"><input id="vmc-hide-same" type="checkbox" checked /> Hide items that are the same</label>
          <button id="vmc-all-left" class="vmt-button" type="button">Use left for every difference</button>
          <button id="vmc-all-right" class="vmt-button" type="button">Use right for every difference</button>
          <button
            id="vmc-all-newest"
            class="vmt-button"
            type="button"
            title="Keeps the copy with the higher version number. When both have the same version number, the left one is kept."
          >Use the newest for every difference</button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div id="vmc-groups" class="vmt-groups"></div>

      <div class="vmt-panel vmt-sticky">
        <div id="vmc-warn" class="vmt-warn" hidden></div>
        <div class="vmt-actions">
          <button id="vmc-download" class="vmt-button vmt-primary" type="button">Download zip</button>
          <button id="vmc-copy" class="vmt-button" type="button">Copy the merged code</button>
          <span id="vmc-out" class="vmt-status"></span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>What you see</h2>

  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Label</th><th>Meaning</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><strong>only left</strong> / <strong>only right</strong></td><td>Saved in one code and missing from the other. Kept unless you untick it.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>different</strong></td><td>Saved in both under the same name, with different contents. Open it to see every field that differs.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>same</strong></td><td>Exactly the same in both. Kept once.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>older version</strong></td><td>You are keeping the copy saved by an older vMenu than the other one.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Picking a side</h2>

  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Choice</th><th>What ends up in the new code</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><strong>Keep left</strong></td><td>The left copy only.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Keep right</strong></td><td>The right copy only.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Keep both</strong></td><td>Both, with one of them saved under a new name. Not available for settings, which only work under their own name.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <p>
    Every item has a version number, which goes up when a newer vMenu changes how that kind of item is
    saved. It says nothing about when you saved it.
  </p>

  <p>
    <strong>Use the newest for every difference</strong> keeps the copy with the higher version number.
    When both copies have the same version number, it keeps the left one, because the page cannot tell
    which of the two you saved last. This is also what every difference starts on when you open the codes.
  </p>

  <h2>Worth knowing</h2>

  <ul>
    <li>Nothing reaches the game until you paste the merged code in under <strong>Misc Settings, Import &amp; Export</strong>.</li>
    <li>
      Keeping an older version is allowed, but <strong>Paste A Code</strong> skips any item where your
      computer already has a newer one. Use <strong>Paste A Code And Replace Everything</strong> if you
      really want the older one.
    </li>
    <li>The zip holds the merged code plus a backup of both codes you pasted in.</li>
    <li>To change items by hand, open the merged code in <a href={`${base}/data-editor/`}>Edit Your Data</a>.</li>
  </ul>
</StarlightPage>

<script>
  import { setup } from '../scripts/data-compare.js';

  setup();
</script>
